Project Idea: Smart E-Commerce Dashboard
Session 1 – Project Orientation & Idea Finalization

Project Overview
The Smart E-Commerce Dashboard is a React-based web application designed to provide a modern and user-friendly shopping experience inspired by platforms such as Flipkart, Amazon, and other popular e-commerce applications. The main goal of the project is to allow users to browse products, search and filter items, view detailed product information, manage a shopping cart, and complete a simple checkout process. The project will also include an admin dashboard for managing products and monitoring basic sales information. The application will focus on reusable React components, state management, API/GraphQL integration, authentication, responsive UI design, and a smooth user journey.
1. Main Goal of the Project
The main goal of the Smart E-Commerce Dashboard is to build a React-based shopping platform where users can easily discover products, search and filter items, view product details, add products to a cart, and complete the checkout process in a simple and responsive interface. The project will combine practical features commonly found in modern e-commerce applications with React concepts such as reusable components, props, state management, conditional rendering, API integration, and user authentication. An admin dashboard will also be included to provide basic product and order management functionality.
2. Five Core Features
No.	Core Feature	Why It Is Important
1	Product Search & Filtering	Users can quickly find products using keywords, categories, price range, ratings, and other filters instead of browsing the entire product catalog.
2	Product Details & Reviews	Users can view product images, description, price, specifications, ratings, and reviews before deciding whether to purchase an item.
3	Shopping Cart	Users can add multiple products, change quantities, remove items, and see the updated cart total before checkout.
4	Wishlist / Favorites	Users can save products they are interested in and return to them later without having to search for them again.
5	Checkout & Order History	Users can complete their purchase through a simple checkout flow and later view their previous and current orders from their account.
